# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not.
#
# Groq API key. A PAID Developer plan is approved for this project (ADR-0008),
# capped at $25/month at the provider. Per-run cost is NOT yet measured: ADR-0008's
# ~$0.067 estimate assumed non-reasoning models and is known to be low. The real
# figure comes from `completion_cost()` once the answer phase runs.
GROQ_API_KEY=

# Master key for the local LiteLLM Proxy in compose.yaml. Any random string;
# it authenticates this machine to its own gateway, not to Groq.
LITELLM_MASTER_KEY=

# Optional: where the LiteLLM gateway listens. Defaults to http://localhost:4010,
# which is what compose.yaml publishes. 4000 is LiteLLM's own default and is
# deliberately avoided -- it is the port any other project's gateway would take.
# LITELLM_PROXY_URL=http://localhost:4010

# There is no third secret to set. The harness does not spend through the master
# key above -- the gateway does not enforce budgets on it (measured; see
# ADR-0009) -- so it derives a budgeted virtual key from it on first use. That
# key appears at the gateway under the alias `fi-rag-eval` with a $25/30d budget.
# Rotating LITELLM_MASTER_KEY rotates it.
